    "qualityRules": [
      "Persuasion principles are structured influence levers—proof, authority, reciprocity, consistency, liking, scarcity—applied transparently in offers and creative.",
      "A value proposition articulates the meaningful benefit a customer gets, for whom, and why the brand wins versus alternatives.",
      "Urgency is a time-based reason to act now—deadlines, limited windows—used honestly to overcome delay.",
      "Scarcity communicates limited quantity or access, raising perceived value and motivating action when accurate.",
      "Social proof uses others’ behavior and testimonials—reviews, counts, UGC—to reduce uncertainty and guide decisions.",
      "Authority persuasion uses expert status, certifications, or credible demonstrators to increase acceptance of claims.",
      "Reciprocity is the tendency to respond to value received with a return favor—used via free education, samples, or tools before the ask.",
      "CTA strategy selects the action, copy, and visual prominence appropriate to awareness level and offer, distinct from pure placement craft in storytelling/video-marketing topics.",
      "Offer presentation structures the commercial offer—price anchoring, bundles, bonuses, guarantees—so value is obvious and objections drop.",
      "Objection handling anticipates buyer doubts—price, efficacy, fit, risk—and answers them with proof and reframing in the creative."
    ],
